^SAMPLE = GSM1626793
!Sample_title = P14 mouse retina 1
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM1626793
!Sample_status = Public on May 20 2015
!Sample_submission_date = Mar 06 2015
!Sample_last_update_date = May 15 2019
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Mus musculus retina, P14
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = strain/background: C57BL/6
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype/variation: wild-type
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: retina
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = age: P14
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Single-cell suspensions were processed through Drop-Seq to generate single-cell cDNA libraries attached to microbeads.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Microbeads were counted, and amplified by PCR, and the 3' end of the cDNA prepared for sequencing using a modified Nextera XT protocol.
!Sample_description = Drop-Seq
!Sample_data_processing = Base calls performed with bcl2fastq2.15.
!Sample_data_processing = Read 2 was aligned with Star v2.4.0.
!Sample_data_processing = Each aligned read was tagged with its mate-pair UMI and cell barcode.
!Sample_data_processing = Each aligned exonic read was tagged with a gene name.
!Sample_data_processing = A digital expression matrix was built by counting the number of unique UMIs per gene within each cell; columns are cells, and rows are genes.
!Sample_data_processing = The first inflection point was estimated on a cumulative sum plot of the digital expression matrix to determine the number of cells in the sample.
!Sample_data_processing = Samples 1-7 -- prepared from P14 mouse retinas on multiple separate days -- were merged together into a single matrix. Merged DGE file from all 7 samples generated.  log(1+10,000*(DGE normalized to total transcripts per cell)) calculated on DGE.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm10 (GRCm38)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Digital expression matrices. Compressed, flat text files with tab delimiters.
